@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2046 = private unnamed_addr constant [636 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for missing whitespace around the equals sign in an unannotated\0Afunction keyword parameter.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAccording to [PEP 8], there should be no spaces around the equals sign in a\0Akeyword parameter, if it is unannotated:\0A\0A> Don\E2\80\99t use spaces around the = sign when used to indicate a keyword\0A> argument, or when used to indicate a default value for an unannotated\0A> function parameter.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef add(a = 0) -> int:\0A    return a + 1\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef add(a=0) -> int:\0A    return a + 1\0A```\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#whitespace-in-expressions-and-statements\0A", align 1
