@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2111 = private unnamed_addr constant [450 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for duplicate base classes in class definitions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIncluding duplicate base classes will raise a `TypeError` at runtime.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass Foo:\0A    pass\0A\0A\0Aclass Bar(Foo, Foo):\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aclass Foo:\0A    pass\0A\0A\0Aclass Bar(Foo):\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Class definitions](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#class-definitions)\0A", align 1
