@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2118 = private unnamed_addr constant [652 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `len` calls on sequences in a boolean test context.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AEmpty sequences are considered false in a boolean context.\0AYou can either remove the call to `len`\0Aor compare the length against a scalar.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afruits = [\22orange\22, \22apple\22]\0Avegetables = []\0A\0Aif len(fruits):\0A    print(fruits)\0A\0Aif not len(vegetables):\0A    print(vegetables)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afruits = [\22orange\22, \22apple\22]\0Avegetables = []\0A\0Aif fruits:\0A    print(fruits)\0A\0Aif not vegetables:\0A    print(vegetables)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A[PEP 8: Programming Recommendations](https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#programming-recommendations)\0A", align 1
